cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: geometres
abstract: >-
  Exact, non-constructive computational geometry over f64 coordinates in
  Rust. The crate provides validated geometry types, the complete DE-9IM
  matrix and the OGC predicates derived from it, validation that reports
  every invalidity, and measurements whose sign is certified and whose
  magnitude carries a documented bound. Every sign decision is an exact
  predicate from arithmetica, so no predicate returns a plausible wrong
  answer on near-degenerate input. No public function returns a coordinate
  that is not an input coordinate, and every simplification is vouched for
  exactly or refused. The crate also covers convex and concave hulls,
  Delaunay triangulation, coverage validation, Hausdorff and Frechet
  distances, prepared polygonal masks, spatial indexing over polygon parts
  and edges, and a deterministic binary codec that is exact on round trip.
authors:
  - family-names: Erlick
    given-names: Justin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5545-0158"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - computational geometry
  - DE-9IM
  - topological predicates
  - exact arithmetic
  - geometry validation
  - Rust